0016:     Expand the colored runs from the left reference panel into the blank right panel.
0017: 
0018:     Input structure:
0019:     - A uniform rectangular frame surrounds the grid.
0020:     - One full-height divider of the frame color splits a left reference panel
0021:       from a blank right panel.
0022:     - Both panels have one background margin column on each side of their active
0023:       columns; the left active columns contain two-column endpoint slots, possibly
0024:       connected by same-color horizontal runs.
0025: 
0026:     Rule:
0027:     - Keep the original grid and paint only in the right panel's active columns.
0028:     - A source run exactly matching the left endpoint slot is copied to the left
0029:       two columns of the right active span.
0030:     - A source run exactly matching the right endpoint slot is copied to the right
0031:       two columns of the right active span.
0032:     - A source run connecting the endpoint slots is stretched across the entire
0033:       right active span.
0034: 
0035:     Key insight:
0036:     The left panel is a compressed legend for the right panel: endpoint markers
0037:     stay two pixels wide, while connectors between endpoints expand to fill the
0038:     distance between them.
0039:     """
0040:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0041:     assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
