0015: def main(input_grid):
0016:     """
0017:     Complete each partial object by scaling and recoloring the largest template so its indicator aligns with the partial indicator.
0018: 
0019:     Input structure:
0020:     - The grid contains several two-color objects on a black background.
0021:     - One indicator color appears in every object.
0022:     - One object is the full template; the others are partial scaled objects with their own colors.
0023: 
0024:     Rule:
0025:     - Find the common indicator color across all objects.
0026:     - Choose the template by largest object size normalized by indicator size.
0027:     - Scale and recolor the template for each other object, then paste it with indicators aligned.
0028: 
0029:     Key insight:
0030:     - The indicator region supplies both correspondence and scale, while the template supplies
0031:       the missing shape around each partial object.
0032:     """
0033:     # Plan:
0034:     # 1. Parse the input into template object and other objects, and determine the indicator color
0035:     # 2. For each other object, rescale+recolor the template to match indicators
0036: 
0037:     # 1. Parse the input
0038: 
0039:     # Extract all the objects from the input grid
